<section class="eg-page-hero"><div class="eg-container"><div class="eg-breadcrumb"><a href="/ezgraph/compare/langgraph/">Compare the layers</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>QuoteGraph</div><span class="eg-eyebrow">One application comparison</span><h1>Less application plumbing.<br>Inspect the evidence.</h1><p class="eg-lede">QuoteGraph and QuoteLanggraph implement an insurance quote journey with five stages, validation, corrections, deterministic rating, and acceptance. This case compares the application code in those two implementations.</p><p class="eg-note">Measurement snapshot: October 9, 2026. Source file hashes and raw counts are included in the <a href="/assets/ezgraph/quotegraph-code-counts.json" download>downloadable inventory</a>.</p></div></section>
<nav class="eg-container eg-page-nav" aria-label="Case study sections"><a href="#headline">Counts and scope</a><a href="#concerns">Where code moves</a><a href="#modularity">Modularity</a><a href="#patterns">Tool handling</a><a href="#method">Method and limits</a><a href="#references">Sources</a></nav>
<section class="eg-article-section" id="headline"><div class="eg-container eg-split"><div><span class="eg-eyebrow">The measured result</span><h2>{{ ezgraphEvidence.reduction }}% fewer application lines in this example.</h2><p>EZGraph: <strong>{{ ezgraphEvidence.ezgraphLines }}</strong> normalized graph-application lines. Direct LangGraph: <strong>{{ ezgraphEvidence.langgraphLines }}</strong>. The difference is <strong>{{ ezgraphEvidence.difference }}</strong> lines under the stated method.</p><p>These are application-maintained lines. Both runtime libraries are excluded. The shared backend implementations are measured separately at 287 normalized lines each; controllers, prompts, tests, and configuration are outside the headline.</p><p class="eg-note">The result measures code size in these implementations. It does not measure developer time, runtime performance, model accuracy, or reliability.</p></div><div class="eg-evidence"><div class="eg-evidence-heading">Normalized graph-application lines</div><div class="eg-meter"><div class="eg-meter-label"><span>EZGraph application</span><b>{{ ezgraphEvidence.ezgraphLines }}</b></div><div class="eg-meter-track"><div class="eg-meter-fill" style="width:{{ ezgraphEvidence.barWidth }}%"></div></div></div><div class="eg-meter"><div class="eg-meter-label"><span>Direct LangGraph application</span><b>{{ ezgraphEvidence.langgraphLines }}</b></div><div class="eg-meter-track"><div class="eg-meter-fill eg-meter-fill-muted"></div></div></div><p class="eg-note">7 EZGraph graph files; 4 direct LangGraph graph/session files. Different organization contributes to the count.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-article-section" id="concerns"><div class="eg-container"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Application responsibilities</span><h2>What the supplied layer absorbs.</h2><div class="eg-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Where the application code moves"><table><thead><tr><th>Responsibility</th><th>EZGraph application</th><th>Direct comparison application</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Model/tool rounds</td><td>Nodes declare prompts and tools; the runtime handles common rounds and dispatch.</td><td>The graph class maintains its own model invocation and dispatch loop.</td></tr>
<tr><td>State and history</td><td>Typed node channels and named history spaces follow the runtime contract.</td><td>The application maintains state shape and stage/history bookkeeping.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Transitions and responses</td><td>Handlers return shared outcomes such as <code>go()</code>, <code>direct()</code>, and <code>finish()</code>.</td><td>The application implements response selection and routing around its stage logic.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Session lifecycle</td><td>The engine coordinates restore, invocation, and persistence.</td><td>A dedicated application session-store module and invocation path supply that behavior.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Domain policy</td><td>Validation, catalog matching, rating, and acceptance remain application code.</td><td>The same kinds of domain responsibilities remain application code.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p style="margin-top:25px">The integration is the point: one contract connects these responsibilities across stages. A team can also extract reusable helpers in its direct LangGraph application.</p></div></section>
<section class="eg-article-section" id="modularity"><div class="eg-container"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Structure you can navigate</span><h2>Find a stage's responsibilities in its node.</h2><p>The EZGraph application has a graph definition, a state registry, and five stage files. The direct implementation places most graph behavior in one graph class, with separate state, types, and session-store modules. File organization is a choice, and it affects this result.</p><p>A driver validation change belongs in <code>DriverNode</code>. A graph-wide model default belongs in the graph definition. History sharing is declared in <code>historySpaces</code>. This supplies an established location for each concern across EZGraph applications.</p><div class="eg-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Measured EZGraph graph file inventory"><table><thead><tr><th>EZGraph file</th><th>Normalized lines</th><th>Raw lines</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for file, counts in ezgraphEvidence.quoteGraph.files %}<tr><td><code>{{ file }}</code></td><td>{{ counts.normalized }}</td><td>{{ counts.raw }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div><h3>Direct LangGraph application inventory</h3><div class="eg-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Measured direct LangGraph graph file inventory"><table><thead><tr><th>Direct LangGraph file</th><th>Normalized lines</th><th>Raw lines</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for file, counts in ezgraphEvidence.quoteLanggraph.files %}<tr><td><code>{{ file }}</code></td><td>{{ counts.normalized }}</td><td>{{ counts.raw }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div><p class="eg-note" style="margin-top:20px">Separately counted controllers: 47 versus 74 normalized lines. Backend helpers: 287 versus 287. Full paths, hashes, and counts are in the snapshot.</p></div></section>
<section class="eg-article-section" id="patterns"><div class="eg-container eg-narrow"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Compare behavior as well as code</span><h2>A shorter loop needs a precise contract.</h2><p>EZGraph centralizes tool schema validation, corrective results, dispatch, outcomes, and diagnostics. The direct application demonstrates the code needed for its chosen loop and session design.</p><div class="eg-callout"><strong>The two loops have a material difference.</strong><p>The direct comparison selects the first tool call from a model candidate. EZGraph supports its defined batch behavior. The implementations share a product journey, but this evidence does not establish complete behavioral parity for multi-tool candidates.</p></div><p>A modern LangGraph application can compose LangChain agents and middleware rather than write every model/tool round by hand. An equivalent baseline using those helpers has not been counted here. This case demonstrates this repository's applications; it does not establish the smallest possible LangGraph implementation.</p><a class="eg-link" href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/middleware/overview">Read the upstream composition options ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="eg-article-section" id="method"><div class="eg-container eg-narrow"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Method and limitations</span><h2>Reproduce the number, then assess the fit.</h2><p>The measurement script excludes blank lines, full-line comments, and imports from selected TypeScript files. It counts the remaining physical lines. Formatting choices still matter; this is not an abstract syntax or complexity metric.</p><p>The selected files cover graph definitions, node/stage behavior, state definitions, and the comparison's session/type modules. The headline excludes runtime libraries, prompts, controllers, tests, configuration, and backend helpers.</p><div class="eg-terminal"><div class="eg-terminal-label">In a pico-web checkout with an ezgraph-demo sibling</div><pre><code>node scripts/ezgraph-compare-metrics.mjs ../ezgraph-demo</code></pre></div><p>The snapshot records the measurement date, repository base revision, and SHA-256 hashes for each measured file. Match the hashes when reproducing this particular result; a moving branch may contain newer application code.</p><ul class="eg-source-list"><li>The baseline is a specific direct implementation, with its own organization and helper choices.</li><li>Shared backend counts do not establish complete semantic equivalence.</li><li>Runtime size and the work performed inside EZGraph are outside the count.</li><li>No development-time, performance, reliability, or adoption experiment is represented by this number.</li></ul><a class="eg-link" href="/assets/ezgraph/quotegraph-code-counts.json" download>Download the complete measurement snapshot <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></section>
